    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-102342",
      "summary": "The following SVG will produce a link with a `javascript` scheme. If the user clicks this link, they will run it.\n\n```svg\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <a>\n    <set attributeName=\"href\" to=\"javascript:alert('SET_XSS')\"></set>\n    <text y=\"30\">Click set</text>\n  </a>\n</svg>\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nAllows stored XSS in applications that allow the `animate` and `set` tags.\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in 3.3.3, 4.0.3, and 4.1.4\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDo not enable the `animate` or `set` tags.",
      "cvssScore": 5.4,
      "severity": "Medium",
      "published": "2026-09-29",
      "modified": "2026-09-29",
      "cwe": {
        "cwe_id": "CWE-79",
